        "subject": "LU-19459 llite: use ATTR_CTIME_SET since v6.17",
        "message": "LU-19459 llite: use ATTR_CTIME_SET since v6.17\n\nAn ATTR_CTIME_SET flag was finally added in upstream kernel\ncommit v6.17-rc7-14-gafc5b36e29 and can be used directly as it\nwas in the past, instead of our own flag OP_XVALID_CTIME_SET.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 3a6bbda288 (\"LU-10030 clio: don't use spare bits in iattr.ia_valid\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ife1561717f6bf7f48a9dba97c41ae9e9103ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65898\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
